      "claim": "Overnight return predicts the opposite first half-hour return in US index ETFs; stronger in volatile periods, weaker after the 2010s; absent in non-US index ETFs."
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": {
    "behavior": "Overnight retail buying/selling is unwound by arbitrageurs in the first 30 minutes, so the gap partly reverses.",
    "failure_theory": [
      "Effect reported weaker after the 2010s.",
      "Gao et al. 2018 found first half-hour momentum into the last half-hour, a different horizon but opposite flavour.",
      "Costs and the 0.75% stop may erase a small edge."
    ]
  },
